Source landscape: China’s 2023 welfare record for Xi Jinping is best covered by a mix of official statistical communiqués, sector ministry bulletins, UN/IGO country reports, treaty-body observations, and a smaller set of NGO and World Bank/ILO analyses. The strongest documentary families here are health insurance and service-access statistics, education spending and enrollment data, social assistance and minimum-living-support notices, child/disability rights treaty materials, migrant worker and care-work studies, and food-security / human-development assessments. I found more than 30 distinct candidate documents and kept both favorable and adverse lines of inquiry.

